/*
class Node {
    int data;
    Node left, right;

    Node(int val) {
        data = val;
        left = right = null;
    }
}
*/

class Solution {
       
    static int preIndx;                                                     // Tracks current index in preorder
     
    static Node Tree(int inorder[], int preorder[], int s, int e) {
        
        if(s > e){ return null;}                                            // Base case: invalid range
        
        Node root = new Node(preorder[preIndx++]);                          // Create root node from preorder
        
        int inIndx=s;
        for(int i=s;i<=e;i++){                                              // Find root index in inorder
            if(inorder[i] == root.data){
                inIndx = i;
                break;
            }
        }
        
        root.left = Tree(inorder, preorder, s, inIndx-1);                   // Recursively build left subtree
        root.right = Tree(inorder, preorder,inIndx+1, e);                   // Recursively build right subtree
        
        return root;                                                        // Return constructed root
        
    }
        
    public static Node buildTree(int inorder[], int preorder[]) {
        int n = inorder.length-1;
        preIndx = 0;                                                        // Reset preorder index
         
        return Tree(inorder,preorder,0,n);                                  // Start building from full range
        
    }

}

//////////////////////// DRY RUN /////////////////////////////

Example: inorder = [3, 1, 4, 0, 5, 2], preorder = [0, 1, 3, 4, 2, 5]

Step 1: preIndx=0, root=0 (preorder[0])
        inorder index of 0 = 3
        Left: [3,1,4], Right: [5,2]

Step 2: preIndx=1, root=1 (preorder[1])
        inorder index of 1 = 1
        Left: [3], Right: [4]

Step 3: preIndx=2, root=3 (preorder[2]) → leaf
Step 4: preIndx=3, root=4 (preorder[3]) → leaf

Step 5: preIndx=4, root=2 (preorder[4])
        inorder index of 2 = 5
        Left: [5], Right: []

Step 6: preIndx=5, root=5 (preorder[5]) → leaf

Tree constructed:
        0
       / \
      1   2
     / \  /
    3  4 5

Output: [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5]

//////////////////////// QUESTION ////////////////////////////

Construct Tree from Inorder & Preorder
Given two arrays representing the inorder and preorder traversals of a binary tree, construct the binary tree and return its root.
Note: Arrays contain unique values, and every value in preorder is also in inorder.

Examples:

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Input: inorder[] = [3, 1, 4, 0, 5, 2], preorder[] = [0, 1, 3, 4, 2, 5]

        0
       / \
      1   2
     / \  /
    3  4 5

Output: [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5]

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Input: inorder[] = [2, 5, 4, 1, 3], preorder[] = [1, 4, 5, 2, 3]

      1
     / \
    4   3
   /
  5
 /
2

Output: [1, 4, 3, 5, N, N, N, 2]

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Constraints:
• 1 ≤ number of nodes ≤ 10^3
• 0 ≤ nodes->data ≤ 10^3
• Both arrays contain unique values
